# One line ending everywhere: LF, in the repository and in the working copy,
# whatever core.autocrlf says. Git for Windows ships autocrlf=true, which
# checked files out as CRLF and warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF" every
# time a tool (npx cap sync, an editor, a script) wrote a file with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe needs CRLF to run a batch file reliably.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
